This confirms an active local tty1 admin login and its PAM/logind session. The guest's displayed current UTC time, journal timestamp, and rounded idle time are inconsistent; this capture does not claim when the login began. It did not initiate a new login.

## Plasma/Wayland readiness and runtime state

Commands included:

```sh
systemctl --user cat plasma-kwin_wayland.service
systemctl --user show plasma-kwin_wayland.service -p FragmentPath -p DropInPaths -p ExecStart -p ActiveState
ls -l /usr/share/wayland-sessions /opt/kf6/bin/startplasma-wayland /usr/lib/systemd/user/plasma-kwin_wayland.service /etc/systemd/user/plasma-kwin_wayland.service.d/10-wayland-only.conf
find /opt/kf6/share /usr/share -maxdepth 4 -type f -iname '*plasma*.desktop'
pgrep -a -u admin 'kwin|plasmashell|startplasma|ksmserver'
```

Observed:

```text
# /usr/lib/systemd/user/plasma-kwin_wayland.service
ExecStart=/opt/kf6/bin/kwin_wayland_wrapper --xwayland
# /etc/systemd/user/plasma-kwin_wayland.service.d/10-wayland-only.conf
