-rwxr-xr-x 1 root root 327272 Sep 23 08:13 /opt/kf6/bin/startplasma-wayland
lrwxrwxrwx 1 root root 53 Sep 23 22:20 /usr/lib/systemd/user/plasma-kwin_wayland.service -> /opt/kf6/lib/systemd/user/plasma-kwin_wayland.service
/opt/kf6/share/wayland-sessions/plasma.desktop
/opt/kf6/share/xsessions/plasmax11.desktop
```

`plasma.desktop` has `Exec=/opt/kf6/libexec/plasma-dbus-run-session-if-needed /opt/kf6/bin/startplasma-wayland` and `DesktopNames=KDE`. `/dev/dri/card0` exists. The admin user's own systemd user manager could not be queried: `sudo -n -u admin ... systemctl --user show ...` returned `sudo: a password is required`. The successful `systemctl --user cat/show` above queried the SSH caller's (`sa`) user manager; its loaded fragment/drop-in/ExecStart are recorded, but this is not represented as an admin-manager query.

No `kwin_wayland`, `plasmashell`, or `startplasma-wayland` process was listed for admin. No graphical session was started or visually observed. The CUA surface still reports `apps: []`; it cannot provide control/observation of the already-running Hyper-V VMConnect windows. Next evidence gate is a real Plasma session on the guest console, with `loginctl` reporting its Wayland session and the runtime observed on that console.
